[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/382898644","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/4943#issuecomment-382898644","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/4943","id":382898644,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM4Mjg5ODY0NA==","user":{"login":"ilevkivskyi","id":12005495,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDA1NDk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12005495?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi","html_url":"https://github.com/ilevkivskyi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-04-19T22:21:21Z","updated_at":"2018-04-19T22:21:21Z","body":"Thanks for reporting! What you show here is not a good repro, it is hard to imagine code that does this:\r\n```python\r\nself.string_union_param = 'this is a string'  # type: Union[str, StringDescriptor]\r\n```\r\nTBH I would say we should just prohibit such code :-) A more realistic, and a simpler repro is below:\r\n```python\r\nclass String:\r\n    def __get__(self, inst, owner) -> str:\r\n        ...\r\n\r\nclass A:\r\n    attr: str\r\n\r\nclass B:\r\n    attr = String()\r\n\r\nx: Union[A, B]\r\n\r\nreveal_type(x.attr) # Revealed type is 'Union[builtins.str, tstd.String]'\r\n```\r\nWhile the latter should be just `builtins.str`. The reason is trivial, unions are just ignored in `analyze_descriptor_access`:\r\n```python\r\n        if not isinstance(descriptor_type, Instance):\r\n            return descriptor_type\r\n```\r\nInstead this function just should map the rest of the logic over the elements of the union. Thus this is easy to fix.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/382898644/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ilevkivskyi","id":12005495,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDA1NDk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12005495?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi","html_url":"https://github.com/ilevkivskyi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":1585007273,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE1ODUwMDcyNzM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/events/1585007273","actor":{"login":"ilevkivskyi","id":12005495,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDA1NDk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12005495?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi","html_url":"https://github.com/ilevkivskyi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilev